<h1>Your company briefing</h1>
<p id="message" role="status"></p>

<section class="card">
  <h2>1. Choose your focus</h2>

  <form id="company-form">
    <label>
      Company name
      <input name="name" required maxlength="100" />
    </label>

    <label>
      Company domain
      <input name="domain" required placeholder="example.com" />
    </label>

    <label>
      Industry
      <input name="industry" required maxlength="100"
             placeholder="Industrial robotics" />
    </label>

    <label>
      Keyword 1
      <input name="keyword1" required maxlength="60"
             placeholder="warehouse automation" />
    </label>

    <label>
      Keyword 2
      <input name="keyword2" required maxlength="60"
             placeholder="grippers" />
    </label>

    <label>
      Briefing language
      <select name="language">
        <option value="en">English</option>
        <option value="es">Spanish</option>
        <option value="fr">French</option>
        <option value="de">German</option>
      </select>
    </label>

    <p class="small">
      One industry and two keywords. Three stories a day are written from them.
    </p>

    <button type="button" id="suggest">Suggest topics</button>
    <button>Save and prepare preview</button>
  </form>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>2. Preview and activate</h2>

  <div id="preview">Save your topics to prepare a preview.</div>

  <button id="refresh-preview">Refresh preview</button>

  <p id="billing-status"></p>
  <p id="comped-note" class="small ok" hidden></p>

  <button id="checkout" hidden>Activate for $25/month with PayPal →</button>
  <button id="cancel" hidden>Cancel renewal</button>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>3. Add your stakeholders</h2>

  <p>
    Your feed publishes once 10 people from your company are on board — you
    plus 9 colleagues. Getting the right stakeholders reading the briefing is
    what makes it useful across the business.
  </p>

  <p id="stakeholder-state" class="small"></p>

  <p class="small">
    Add as many recipients as you like beyond the first 10. Every issue carries
    a one-click unsubscribe, and an address that opts out or bounces is
    suppressed across the whole platform and cannot be re-added.
  </p>

  <form id="invite-form">
    <label>
      Stakeholder email
      <input name="email" type="email" required />
    </label>

    <label class="check">
      <input name="authorised" type="checkbox" required />
      I have the authority to add this person to this list and to send them
      this newsletter.
    </label>

    <button>Add recipient</button>
  </form>

  <ul id="subscribers"></ul>
</section>

<section class="card" id="site-card">
  <h2>4. Your site</h2>

  <p>
    Your briefing has its own address. Readers, the RSS feed and the embed all
    live there — brand it with your name, or put it on a domain you own.
  </p>

  <p id="site-address" class="site-address"></p>

  <form id="subdomain-form">
    <label>
      Subdomain
      <span class="affix">
        <input name="subdomain" required minlength="3" maxlength="63"
               pattern="[a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]*[a-z0-9])?"
               autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" />
        <span class="suffix" id="sites-domain"></span>
      </span>
    </label>

    <p class="small" id="rename-note"></p>

    <button>Rename</button>
  </form>

  <h3>Custom domain <span id="plan-badge" class="badge" hidden></span></h3>

  <p class="small" id="domain-intro">
    Point a hostname you control at your site — <code>news.yourcompany.com</code>
    or <code>www.yourcompany.com</code>. Add it here, then create the DNS
    record shown. It goes live the moment the record is visible.
  </p>

  <form id="domain-form">
    <label>
      Hostname
      <input name="hostname" placeholder="news.yourcompany.com" required
             maxlength="253" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" />
    </label>

    <button>Use this domain</button>
  </form>

  <div id="domain-status" hidden>
    <p id="domain-state" class="small"></p>

    <table class="dns">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Type</th><th>Name</th><th>Value</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody id="dns-rows"></tbody>
    </table>

    <p class="small">
      The CNAME both routes traffic and verifies the domain. If your DNS
      provider proxies or flattens CNAMEs, add the TXT record as well.
    </p>

    <button type="button" id="verify-domain">Check DNS now</button>
    <button type="button" id="remove-domain">Remove domain</button>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>Publish your feed</h2>

  <p id="publish-state" class="small"></p>

  <p id="feed-links"></p>

  <label>
    Iframe embed
    <textarea id="embed-code" readonly></textarea>
  </label>

  <button id="copy-digest">Copy branded digest</button>
</section>

<section class="card" id="password-card">
  <h2>Password</h2>

  <p class="small" id="password-state"></p>

  <form id="password-form">
    <label id="current-label" hidden>
      Current password
      <input name="current" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" />
    </label>

    <label>
      <span id="password-label">New password</span>
      <input name="password" type="password" minlength="8"
             autocomplete="new-password" required />
    </label>

    <p class="small">
      At least 8 characters. Setting or changing it signs out every other
      session. You can always sign in by emailed link instead.
    </p>

    <button>Save password</button>
    <button type="button" id="remove-password" hidden>Remove password</button>
  </form>
</section>

<button id="logout">Sign out</button>

<script src="/app.js" defer></script>
